    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>This is a game that requires 2 players and 2 controllers to play</strong> <br><br>Key Features:\u00a0</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Track Customization</strong>\u00a0-\u00a0 The Track in this game is a randomly generated tile based system, there is also options the player can turn on and off, like the corners and jumps.<br>All of the buildings on the track also have random elements</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>2 Game-Modes -</strong> There are 2 playable game-modes in this game, <strong>the Runner and Chaser game-mode</strong> has one of the players playing as the Runner, which means their goal is to get away from the Runner and make it to the end of the track, whilst the Chaser's goal is to chase the other player down, the Chaser is quicker so there are Power-Ups and Traps the Runner can use to slow the Chaser down <br>There is also a <strong>Standard Race game-mode</strong>, where both player start with the same speed and both have access to the Power-Ups with each player's goal being to reach the end-line first</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Customisable Game Parameters</strong> - Include the number of games, the track length, who is the Runner and Chaser\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>This is a game that requires 2 players and 2 controllers to play</strong> <br><br>Key Features:\u00a0</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Track Customization</strong>\u00a0-\u00a0 The Track in this game is a randomly generated tile based system, there is also options the player can turn on and off, like the corners and jumps.<br>All of the buildings on the track also have random elements</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>2 Game-Modes -</strong> There are 2 playable game-modes in this game, <strong>the Runner and Chaser game-mode</strong> has one of the players playing as the Runner, which means their goal is to get away from the Runner and make it to the end of the track, whilst the Chaser's goal is to chase the other player down, the Chaser is quicker so there are Power-Ups and Traps the Runner can use to slow the Chaser down <br>There is also a <strong>Standard Race game-mode</strong>, where both player start with the same speed and both have access to the Power-Ups with each player's goal being to reach the end-line first</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Customisable Game Parameters</strong> - Include the number of games, the track length, who is the Runner and Chaser\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Welcome to Duel Drive, a thrilling split-screen racing experience that plunges you into a neon-soaked cyberpunk world. Master the art of hover car racing with unique physics and responsive controls and experience the adrenaline rush of racing head-to-head with friends in dynamic split-screen",
